sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Developer
    participant Agent as AI Agent (Claude)
    participant FS as File System

    User->>Agent: Run /vista:plan <feature-name>
    Note over Agent: Plan workflow begins,<br>domain requirements and specs gathered

    Agent->>FS: Create arch/ directory in .vista/features/<name>/

    Note over Agent: Choose best format per diagram type

    Agent->>FS: Write .mmd files (flowcharts, sequences, ER, state)
    Note over FS: system-architecture.mmd<br>user-flow.mmd<br>sequence-*.mmd

    opt Hardware/network diagrams needed
        Agent->>FS: Write .puml files (nwdiag, component)
        Note over FS: network-topology.puml<br>component-layout.puml
    end

    opt Infrastructure/rack diagrams needed
        Agent->>FS: Write .d2 files (spatial layouts)
        Note over FS: infrastructure.d2<br>rack-diagram.d2
    end

    opt Freeform spatial diagrams needed
        Agent->>FS: Write .excalidraw files (hand-drawn style)
        Note over FS: hardware-layout.excalidraw
    end

    opt Quick text diagrams
        Agent->>FS: Write .txt files (ASCII art)
        Note over FS: pinout.txt<br>bus-timing.txt
    end

    Agent->>FS: Write _arch.json manifest
    Note over FS: Manifest references all diagram files<br>with correct type field per format

    Agent->>FS: Write _plan.json with architecture.ref
    Note over FS: Plan has meta, architecture.ref → ./arch/_arch.json,<br>and implementationPhases
